//!
//! # Regex
//!
//! Regular expressions with linear-time matching, in the style of RE2: a
//! pattern is parsed into an AST, compiled to a program and run by a Pike VM
//! that simulates the NFA, so matching takes O(text x program) time and never
//! backtracks.
//!
//! ```ignis
//! import Captures, Match, Regex from "std::regex";
//!
//! let regex: Regex = Regex::new("\\d+").unwrap();
//! let found: Match = regex.find("abc 123").unwrap(); // 4..7
//!
//! let date: Regex = Regex::new("(?<year>\\d{4})-(\\d\\d)").unwrap();
//! let captures: Captures = date.captures("on 2024-05").unwrap();
//! let year: Match = captures.name("year").unwrap(); // 3..7
//! let swapped: String = date.replaceAll("on 2024-05", "$2/${year}"); // "on 05/2024"
//! let parts: Vector<String> = Regex::new("\\s*,\\s*").unwrap().split("a , b,c"); // a, b, c
//! ```
//!
//! ## Matching
//!
//! - Leftmost-first: of the matches starting at the leftmost position, the
//!   one the pattern prefers wins. Alternatives are tried in order (`a|ab`
//!   on `"ab"` matches `"a"`), greedy repetition prefers more and lazy
//!   repetition fewer.
//! - The search is unanchored unless the pattern uses `^`.
//! - Offsets are byte offsets into the UTF-8 text and always fall on scalar
//!   boundaries. An invalid byte is read as U+FFFD and spans one byte.
//! - `findAll` returns non-overlapping matches; after an empty match it
//!   resumes one scalar further on, so `a*` on `"baa"` gives `0..0`,
//!   `1..3` and `3..3`.
//! - Group 0 is the whole match; group `n` is the `n`-th `(`. A group that
//!   did not take part in the match is `NONE` (`(a)|(b)` on `"b"`: group 1
//!   `NONE`, group 2 `0..1`), and a group in a repetition holds its last
//!   iteration (`(a|b)+` on `"ab"`: group 1 `1..2`).
//! - `replaceAll`, `split` and `capturesAll` use the matches `findAll`
//!   finds, so `x*` replaced by `-` in `"abc"` gives `"-a-b-c-"`.
//! - Matching takes O(text x program) time: the VM runs every thread in
//!   lockstep and follows each instruction at most once per position, so
//!   patterns such as `(a*)*b` cannot backtrack.
//!
//! ## Replacement
//!
//! In the replacement text of `replace` and `replaceAll`:
//!
//! - `$n`, one or more digits read greedily (`$12` is group 12), and `${n}`
//!   insert group `n`; `${1}0` is group 1 followed by `0`.
//! - `${name}` inserts the named group. Braces hold `[A-Za-z0-9_]+`: all
//!   digits is a number, anything else a name.
//! - A group that did not take part or does not exist inserts nothing.
//! - `$$` is a literal `$`; any other `$` (`$x`, `${}`, `${a b}`, a final
//!   `$`) is a literal `$`.
//!
//! ## Limits
//!
//! Counted repetition copies its body, so a program holds at most
//! `REGEX_MAX_PROGRAM` (100000) instructions; a larger one is
//! `pattern too large` at column 1.
//!
//! ## Exports
//!
//! | Export                 | Description                                                    |
//! |------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `Regex`                | `Regex::new(pattern)`: `Result<Regex, RegexError>`; `isMatch(text)`, `find(text)`: `Option<Match>`, `findAll(text)`: `Vector<Match>`, `captures(text)`: `Option<Captures>`, `capturesAll(text)`: `Vector<Captures>`, `replace(text, replacement)` and `replaceAll(text, replacement)`: `String`, `split(text)`: `Vector<String>`, `groupCount()`, `groupName(index)`: `Option<String>`, `groupIndex(name)`: `Option<u64>` |
//! | `Captures`             | `group(index)` and `name(name)`: `Option<Match>`, `whole()`: `Match`, `groupCount()` (whole match excluded), `length()` (included) |
//! | `Match`                | `start()`, `end()`, `length()` in bytes, `isEmpty()`, `textIn(haystack)`: a copy of the matched text |
//! | `REGEX_MAX_PROGRAM`    | The most instructions a compiled pattern may hold: 100000      |
//! | `parseRegex`           | `parseRegex(pattern)`: `Result<RegexAst, RegexError>`          |
//! | `RegexError`           | `column()` (1-based, in Unicode scalars), `message()`, `toString()` |
//! | `RegexAst`             | `nodes`, `root`, `groupCount`                                  |
//! | `RegexNode`            | `EMPTY`, `LITERAL`, `ANY_EXCEPT_NEWLINE`, `CLASS`, `CONCAT`, `ALTERNATE`, `REPEAT`, `GROUP`, `ASSERT` |
//! | `RegexClass`           | Sorted, merged `ranges` and `negated`                          |
//! | `RegexRange`           | Inclusive `start` and `end` scalar values                      |
//! | `RegexRepeat`          | `child`, `min`, `max`, `bounded`, `greedy`                     |
//! | `RegexGroup`           | `child`, `capturing`, `index`, `name`                          |
//! | `RegexAssertion`       | `START`, `END`, `WORD_BOUNDARY`, `NOT_WORD_BOUNDARY`           |
//! | `REGEX_MAX_REPETITION` | The largest count `{n,m}` accepts: 1000                        |
//!
//! ## Syntax
//!
//! | Syntax                            | Meaning                                                  |
//! |-----------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
//! | `x`                               | The scalar `x`, any UTF-8 scalar                         |
//! | `.`                               | Any scalar except `\n`                                   |
//! | `\n` `\t` `\r` `\f` `\v`          | Control scalars                                          |
//! | `\.` `\*` `\\` ...                | Any escaped ASCII punctuation is itself                  |
//! | `[abc]` `[a-z]` `[^...]`          | Classes, ranges, negation; escapes work inside           |
//! | `\d` `\w` `\s` and `\D` `\W` `\S` | `[0-9]`, `[0-9A-Za-z_]`, `[ \t\n\r\f\v]` and negations (ASCII) |
//! | `^` `$`                           | Start and end of the whole text, not of a line           |
//! | `\b` `\B`                         | ASCII word boundary and its negation                     |
//! | `(x)` `(?:x)` `(?<name>x)`        | Capturing, non-capturing and named groups                |
//! | `x\|y`                            | Alternation, leftmost-first                              |
//! | `x*` `x+` `x?`                    | Zero or more, one or more, zero or one                   |
//! | `x{n}` `x{n,}` `x{n,m}`           | Counted repetition, counts at most 1000                  |
//! | `x*?` `x+?` `x??` `x{n,m}?`       | Lazy forms: prefer fewer repetitions                     |
//! | `(?i)` `(?i:x)`                   | ASCII case-insensitive for the rest of the enclosing group, or inside `x` |
//!
//! Group names are `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*` and must be unique. Capturing
//! groups are numbered from 1 in the order of their `(`.
//!
//! The parser is strict where a pattern would otherwise be ambiguous:
//!
//! - `{` always starts a counted repetition; a literal brace is `\{`. A
//!   `{` that is not `{n}`, `{n,}` or `{n,m}` is `invalid repetition`. A
//!   lone `}` or `]` is a literal.
//! - A quantifier after a quantifier (`a**`, `a+*`, `a{2}{3}`) and a
//!   quantifier after `^`, `$`, `\b` or `\B` are `nothing to repeat`; the
//!   `?` of a lazy form is part of its quantifier.
//! - `[]` and `[^]` are `empty class`; a `]` inside a class is `\]`. A `-`
//!   first or last in a class is a literal.
//!
//! ## Errors
//!
//! Every error carries the 1-based column, counted in Unicode scalars, of
//! the part that is wrong: `unclosed group` (at its `(`), `unmatched )`,
//! `nothing to repeat`, `invalid range z-a` (at its `-`), `unclosed class`
//! (at its `[`), `empty class`, `trailing backslash`, `unknown escape \q`,
//! `invalid repetition`, `invalid repetition range`, `repetition count above
//! 1000`, `invalid group name`, `duplicate group name x`, `unknown group
//! flag`, `unsupported: backreference` and `unsupported: lookaround`.
//!
//! Backreferences (`\1`) and lookaround (`(?=`, `(?!`, `(?<=`, `(?<!`) are
//! rejected because they cannot be matched in linear time. Classes are
//! ASCII; Unicode classes are not supported in v1.

import _ from "std::regex::ast";
import _ from "std::regex::parser";
import _ from "std::regex::compiler";
import _ from "std::regex::vm";
import _ from "std::regex::regex";

export
  RegexAssertion,
  RegexAst,
  RegexClass,
  RegexError,
  RegexGroup,
  RegexNode,
  RegexRange,
  RegexRepeat,
from "./ast";
export REGEX_MAX_REPETITION, parseRegex from "./parser";
export REGEX_MAX_PROGRAM from "./compiler";
export Captures, Match, Regex from "./regex";
